@prefix : <http://purl.org/ontoksd#> .
@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rcd: <http://purl.org/ontoksd/rcd#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix ontoksd: <http://purl.org/ontoksd#> .
@base <http://purl.org/ontoksd#> .

<http://purl.org/ontoksd#> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                            owl:versionIRI <http://purl.org/ontoksd#7.0.0> ;
                            owl:imports <http://purl.org/edu/bloom> ,
                                        <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#/1.0.0> ,
                                        <http://purl.org/ontoksd/rcd> ,
                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core.rdf> ;
                            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Anonymous" ;
                            dcterms:description "A OntoKSD é uma ontologia de domínio para representar, especificar, evidenciar e analisar competências educacionais em Educação em Computação. Ela formaliza estruturas de competência baseadas em relações Conhecimento--Habilidade--Disposição, apoiando alinhamento instrucional, evidências avaliativas, interpretação de proficiência e interoperabilidade com referenciais curriculares como CC2020, CS2023 e BNCC Computação."@pt-br ,
                                                "OntoKSD is a domain ontology for representing, specifying, evidencing, and analyzing educational competences in Computing Education. It formalizes competence structures based on Knowledge--Skill--Disposition relations, supports instructional alignment, assessment evidence, proficiency interpretation, and interoperability with curricular frameworks such as CC2020, CS2023, and BNCC Computing."@en ;
                            dcterms:license "<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>" ;
                            dcterms:title "OntoKSD: Ontologia para Especificação de Competências baseadas em Conhecimento--Habilidade--Disposição"@pt-br ,
                                          "OntoKSD: Ontology for Knowledge--Skill--Disposition Competence Specification"@en ;
                            rdfs:comment "Ontology for Knowledge, Skill, and Disposition representation."@en ;
                            rdfs:label "OntoKSD Ontology"@en ;
                            owl:versionInfo 7.0 .

#################################################################
#    Annotation properties
#################################################################

###  http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description
<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation
dcterms:bibliographicCitation rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote
skos:scopeNote rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


#################################################################
#    Datatypes
#################################################################

###  http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date
xsd:date rdf:type rdfs:Datatype .


#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

###  http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#hasReifiedQualityValue
<http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#hasReifiedQualityValue> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#inheresIn
<http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#inheresIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#isComponentOf
<http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#isComponentOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates
<http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#alignedWith
ontoksd:alignedWith rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                    rdfs:range ontoksd:ExternalCompetence ;
                    rdfs:comment """Relates an OntoKSD competence to an externally defined competence with which it presents some recognized semantic, curricular, or referential correspondence. 

This property provides a direct and simplified way to assert external alignment, without by itself specifying the exact nature, strength, or scope of the correspondence. 

It is useful for representing generic links to external frameworks such as BNCC, CC2020, CS2023, or other competence references. When the alignment must be qualified more precisely—such as indicating whether it is equivalent, partial, broader, narrower, contextual, or based on curricular continuity—a dedicated alignment relator or additional alignment metadata should be used.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#appliesKnowledge
ontoksd:appliesKnowledge rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:Skill ;
                         rdfs:range ontoksd:Knowledge ;
                         rdfs:comment """Relates a Skill to a Knowledge element that the specified capability involves applying or mobilizing.

In OntoKSD, appliesKnowledge makes explicit which knowledge content is involved in an explicitly identified skill. It expresses an association within the competence specification rather than an occurrence of knowledge application or evidence of an individual's capability.

The relation does not, by itself, identify a required SkillLevel. Knowledge-specific performance levels are represented through KnowledgeSkill pairings.

A skill may concern multiple knowledge elements, and the same knowledge may be involved in different skills. Shared knowledge does not establish equivalence, composition, specialization, or prerequisite relationships between skills or competences."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#correspondsToLevel
ontoksd:correspondsToLevel rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:ScaleInterval ;
                           rdfs:range ontoksd:ProficiencyLevel ;
                           rdfs:comment """Relates a ScaleInterval to the ProficiencyLevel designated for results within that interval under an identifiable ProficiencyScheme.

In OntoKSD, correspondsToLevel records the intended correspondence between a numeric subrange and a proficiency category. For example, the interval (8.0, 10.0] may correspond to Advanced within a particular scheme.

Each interval used as a classification rule should identify one corresponding level. Its boundaries, endpoint inclusion, associated scale, and applicable scheme must remain explicit. Where identical numeric boundaries have different interpretations in different schemes, separate interval specifications should preserve those correspondences.

The relation documents a basis for interpretation. It does not automatically test score membership, classify a result, assign proficiency to a learner, or establish competence attainment.

This property has domain ScaleInterval and range ProficiencyLevel.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#curricularlyRepresentsKnowledge
ontoksd:curricularlyRepresentsKnowledge rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isCurricularlyRepresentedBy ;
                                        rdfs:domain skos:Concept ;
                                        rdfs:range ontoksd:Knowledge ;
                                        rdfs:comment """Associates a curricular SKOS concept with a Knowledge element whose content it represents within the stated curricular scope.

curricularlyRepresentsKnowledge relates the curricular concept to the Knowledge element; isCurricularlyRepresentedBy expresses the inverse direction. The association preserves the distinction between curricular organization, such as a CS2023 topic, and knowledge content used in an OntoKSD competence specification.

The curricular concept's source and scheme should remain identifiable. Where the correspondence is partial or interpretive, its scope and justification should be documented. Similar labels alone do not establish the association.

A Knowledge element may be represented in multiple curricular structures, and a curricular concept may represent multiple knowledge elements. The relation does not assert identity, exact semantic equivalence, inheritance of curricular classifications, or a required performance level.

Curricular traceability is distinct from an alignment between competence specifications. The association does not, by itself, establish complete curricular coverage or learner attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#definesInterval
ontoksd:definesInterval rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                        owl:inverseOf ontoksd:intervalDefinedInScheme ;
                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:ProficiencyScheme ;
                        rdfs:range ontoksd:ScaleInterval ;
                        rdfs:comment """Associates a ProficiencyScheme with a ScaleInterval adopted for numeric interpretation of assessment results.

definesInterval relates the scheme to the interval; intervalDefinedInScheme expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies the interpretive scheme in which the interval's boundaries and corresponding proficiency category apply.

A numeric scheme may define multiple intervals. Each interval's scale and corresponding ProficiencyLevel should be consistent with that scheme. Where the same numeric boundaries have different interpretations, separate interval specifications should preserve the distinctions.

Qualitative schemes need not define numeric intervals. The association does not, by itself, verify interval coverage, overlaps, gaps, or boundary consistency, nor does it execute score classification or assign learner proficiency.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#definesLevel
ontoksd:definesLevel rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     owl:inverseOf ontoksd:levelDefinedInScheme ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:ProficiencyScheme ;
                     rdfs:range ontoksd:ProficiencyLevel ;
                     rdfs:comment """Associates a ProficiencyScheme with a ProficiencyLevel adopted within its classification structure.

definesLevel relates the scheme to the level; levelDefinedInScheme expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies the scheme that provides the category's meaning through descriptors, criteria, ordering, or numeric interpretation rules.

A scheme defines one or more levels. Identical labels in different schemes do not establish equivalent meanings or comparability. A level should be shared across schemes only where its intended meaning is preserved and documented.

The association defines an available classification category rather than attributing it to a learner. It does not establish equal distances between levels, progression, automatic score classification, or competence attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#derivedFromParticipation
ontoksd:derivedFromParticipation rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                                             ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                                           )
                                             ] ;
                                 rdfs:range ontoksd:AssessmentParticipation ;
                                 rdfs:comment """Relates an EvidencedCompetence or EvidencedCompetenceConstituent record to the AssessmentParticipation grounding its individual evaluative interpretation.

In OntoKSD, each such evidential record refers to exactly one assessment participation. That participation identifies the learner through hasLearner and the assessment occasion through occursInAssessmentOccurrence.

The relation provides participant-level traceability; it does not replace the identification of supporting evidence through supportedByEvidence. Evidence shared within an occurrence does not automatically support every participant's record.

Any learner, profile, or assessment occurrence identified elsewhere in the evidential record should agree with the referenced participation. This property alone does not enforce agreement across those paths or establish the validity of the judgment.

Its domain is the union of EvidencedCompetence and EvidencedCompetenceConstituent, and its range is AssessmentParticipation.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#evidenceBasedOn
ontoksd:evidenceBasedOn rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                        owl:inverseOf ontoksd:producesEvidence ;
                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:Evidence ;
                        rdfs:range ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                        rdfs:comment """Associates an Evidence instance with the AssessmentOccurrence in which it was produced.

evidenceBasedOn relates the evidence to its originating occurrence; producesEvidence expresses the inverse direction. The association records the origin of an artefact or documented observation rather than an assessment specification or an individual judgment.

Evidence may concern individual or collective work. Its production within an occurrence does not automatically attribute it to every participant or establish an identical evidential basis for their judgments. Support for a particular judgment is recorded separately through supportedByEvidence.

An artefact produced before the occurrence must not be assigned that occurrence as its origin merely because it was examined there. A new observation or evaluative record concerning the artefact may originate in the occurrence while preserving the artefact's earlier provenance.

The association does not establish authenticity, validity, sufficiency, or competence attainment."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#evidencesCompetence
ontoksd:evidencesCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            owl:inverseOf ontoksd:supportedByEvidence ;
                            rdfs:domain ontoksd:Evidence ;
                            rdfs:range [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                                       ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                                     )
                                       ] ;
                            rdfs:comment """Associates Evidence with an EvidencedCompetence or EvidencedCompetenceConstituent record whose assessment interpretation it supports.

evidencesCompetence relates the evidence to the supported record; supportedByEvidence expresses the inverse direction. The association concerns a learner-specific, contextualized judgment rather than the reusable Competence or CompetenceConstituent specification.

A record may draw on multiple evidence instances, and the same evidence may support multiple records where its relevance to each interpretation is justified. Shared evidence does not establish identical judgments for different learners, competences, constituents, or occasions.

The evidential basis should remain consistent with the learner, assessment participation, occasion, and applicable criteria identified for the record. Inclusion of evidence in a profile or production within an assessment occurrence does not automatically establish this support relationship.

The association records asserted evidential support. It does not independently establish authenticity, sufficiency, judgment validity, or complete competence attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasAcquisitionContext
ontoksd:hasAcquisitionContext rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isAcquisitionContextOf ;
                              rdfs:domain ontoksd:InstructionalUnit ;
                              rdfs:range ontoksd:AcquisitionContext ;
                              rdfs:comment """Associates an InstructionalUnit with an AcquisitionContext describing the educational circumstances for which the unit is specified.

hasAcquisitionContext relates the instructional unit to its context; isAcquisitionContextOf expresses the inverse direction. Relevant circumstances may include learning modality, available resources, collaboration arrangements, pedagogical support, and environmental or organizational conditions.

The association concerns instructional planning rather than an execution event. Conditions recorded for an AssessmentOccurrence are represented separately through occursInAcquisitionContext and may differ from those anticipated by the instructional specification.

A context may be shared by instructional units where its meaning and boundaries apply consistently. Such sharing does not identify the units as the same entity or establish identical competence qualifications.

The association does not demonstrate that instruction occurred, that anticipated conditions were satisfied, or that competence was acquired.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasActivationConstraint
ontoksd:hasActivationConstraint rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasActivationQualifier ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                                rdfs:range ontoksd:ActivationConstraint ;
                                rdfs:comment """Relates a CompetenceActivation to an ActivationConstraint specifying a condition, limitation, or requirement applicable to that instructional association.

The constraint identifies its content through hasActivationConstraintDescription and its status through hasActivationConstraintType. Multiple conditions may be associated independently, preserving their respective descriptions and classifications.

The association does not replace requirements of the instructional unit that exist independently of competence associations. It does not establish that a condition was satisfied or formally verify compliance.

This property specializes hasActivationQualifier.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasActivationConstraintType
ontoksd:hasActivationConstraintType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:ActivationConstraint ;
                                    rdfs:range ontoksd:ActivationConstraintType ;
                                    rdfs:comment """Associates an ActivationConstraint with the controlled value that classifies the status of its described condition.

In OntoKSD, hasActivationConstraintType has domain ActivationConstraint and range ActivationConstraintType. It distinguishes the classification of a condition, such as mandatory, optional, or conditional, from the condition's textual content recorded through hasActivationConstraintDescription.

Under the adopted class restriction, each ActivationConstraint has exactly one ActivationConstraintType. This single-type policy requires the selected value and the description to provide a coherent interpretation. Where several independently applicable conditions have different statuses, they should be represented as separate constraint instances.

The property relates a constraint specification to its classification. It does not associate the type directly with Competence or CompetenceActivation: an activation references the described constraint through hasActivationConstraint.

Type values are reusable across constraint specifications. Assigning the same type to different constraints does not identify those constraints as the same entity.

The association records intended instructional status rather than applicability to an actual execution or verified compliance. Its cardinality restriction does not, by itself, guarantee that an explicit type value has been recorded in the data; that completeness must be checked separately.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasActivationFunction
ontoksd:hasActivationFunction rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isActivationFunctionOf ;
                              rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                              rdfs:range ontoksd:ActivationFunction ;
                              rdfs:comment """Associates a CompetenceActivation with an ActivationFunction identifying the pedagogical purpose of the competence–instructional unit association.

hasActivationFunction relates the activation to the function value; isActivationFunctionOf expresses the inverse direction. Examples include addressing a competence as an instructional target or presupposing it as a prerequisite, where these distinctions are explicitly adopted.

Function identifies pedagogical purpose rather than the competence's contribution, form of engagement, or applicable conditions, which are represented through role, mode, and constraint qualifications.

Function values are reusable classifications. The same value may qualify multiple activations without identifying those associations as the same entity. Multiple assignments require a coherent interpretation in the instructional specification.

The association records an educational intention or presupposition. It does not establish that instruction occurred, that a learner satisfies a prerequisite, or that competence was attained.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasActivationMode
ontoksd:hasActivationMode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasActivationQualifier ;
                          rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                          rdfs:range ontoksd:ActivationMode ;
                          rdfs:comment """Relates a CompetenceActivation to an ActivationMode classifying the expected form of engagement, such as constructive, analytical, interpretative, or justificatory.

Multiple modes may qualify the same activation without establishing execution order or separate phases. A mode does not automatically determine a SkillLevel or justify changing the competence's required performance.

This property specializes hasActivationQualifier and records expected engagement rather than observed action or competence attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasActivationQualifier
ontoksd:hasActivationQualifier rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                               owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isActivationQualifierOf ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                               rdfs:range ontoksd:ActivationQualifier ;
                               rdfs:comment """Associates a CompetenceActivation with an ActivationQualifier describing the competence's contribution, expected engagement, or applicable conditions within an instructional unit.

hasActivationQualifier relates the activation to its qualifier; isActivationQualifierOf expresses the inverse direction. Specialized associations are represented through hasActivationRole, hasActivationMode, and hasActivationConstraint.

An activation may have multiple qualifiers. Shared values or constraint specifications do not identify distinct activations as the same entity. ActivationFunction is associated separately through hasActivationFunction.

The association qualifies planned instructional use without modifying the competence definition or establishing that the expected performance occurred.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasActivationRole
ontoksd:hasActivationRole rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasActivationQualifier ;
                          rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                          rdfs:range ontoksd:ActivationRole ;
                          rdfs:comment """Relates a CompetenceActivation to an ActivationRole identifying the competence's intended contribution within the instructional unit, such as central, supporting, or transversal.

The role concerns this particular association rather than an intrinsic characteristic of the competence. The same competence may have different roles across instructional units, and role values may be reused across activations.

Role identifies contribution rather than pedagogical purpose, expected engagement, or an applicable condition. A supporting role does not automatically establish a prerequisite, and a central role does not establish that assessment occurred.

This property specializes hasActivationQualifier.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasAlignmentType
ontoksd:hasAlignmentType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:ExternalCompetenceAlignment ;
                         rdfs:range ontoksd:AlignmentType ;
                         rdfs:comment """Relates an ExternalCompetenceAlignment to the AlignmentType identifying its principal correspondence classification.

In OntoKSD, each alignment identifies exactly one principal type. The selected value must be consistent with the compared specifications, the stated scope, and the supporting justification.

Directional types are interpreted from the internal Competence toward the ExternalCompetence. BroaderThanExternalAlignment indicates broader internal coverage; NarrowerThanExternalAlignment indicates a more restricted internal scope.

The classification does not replace the alignment explanation or establish logical equivalence, identity, specialization, complete coverage, regulatory compliance, or learner attainment.

This property has domain ExternalCompetenceAlignment and range AlignmentType.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasAssessmentTypeConcept
ontoksd:hasAssessmentTypeConcept rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:Assessment ;
                                 rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
                                 rdfs:comment """Associates an Assessment with a controlled SKOS concept that classifies an aspect of its evaluative design.

In OntoKSD, hasAssessmentTypeConcept supports classification along dimensions such as assessment agent, modality, and strategy. Each concept should belong to an identifiable concept scheme that makes its classification dimension and intended meaning explicit.

An Assessment may reference multiple concepts from different dimensions where their meanings are compatible. The association does not require the concepts to be represented as subclasses of Assessment or imply that classification values are mutually exclusive.

These classifications concern the assessment specification. For example, a peer-assessment concept describes the planned evaluative arrangement; it does not identify the actual assessor, establish that peer assessment occurred, or record an individual judgment. Actual assessor involvement is represented through hasAssessor on AssessmentParticipation.

This property has domain Assessment and range skos:Concept. Classification does not, by itself, enforce membership in an approved scheme, validate combinations of concepts, or establish compliance with the planned design.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasAssessor
ontoksd:hasAssessor rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentParticipation ;
                    rdfs:range ontoksd:Assessor ;
                    rdfs:comment """Relates an AssessmentParticipation to an Assessor involved in evaluating the identified learner's performance, products, or documented observations in that assessment occurrence.

The association is optional and may identify multiple assessors. The same person may act as both learner and assessor where the evaluative arrangement permits self-assessment.

Identifying an assessor does not establish that the person issued every related judgment, observed all supporting evidence, or validated the result. Responsibility for a specific judgment must be recorded separately where required.

This property has domain AssessmentParticipation and range Assessor. It records evaluator involvement rather than an assessment classification, authorization, or confirmation of judgment validity.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasAttitude
ontoksd:hasAttitude rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                    rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasDisposition ;
                    owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isAttitudeOf ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                    rdfs:range ontoksd:Attitude ;
                    rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence with an Attitude specified as an evaluative orientation relevant to its expected performance.

hasAttitude relates the competence to the attitudinal constituent; isAttitudeOf expresses the inverse direction. The attitude identifies an expected position toward a relevant object, practice, behavior, or situation.

Because Attitude specializes Disposition, hasAttitude specializes hasDisposition, and isAttitudeOf specializes isDispositionOf. An attitudinal association therefore also constitutes a dispositional association. The reverse implication does not hold: a generic disposition does not automatically satisfy an attitude requirement.

The association supports explicit attitudinal requirements, including those of the KSA specification pattern. It does not attribute an attitude to a learner or establish its manifestation, stability, or transfer across contexts.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasBloomLevelJustificationVerb
ontoksd:hasBloomLevelJustificationVerb rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                       rdfs:domain ontoksd:KnowledgeSkill ;
                                       rdfs:range <http://purl.org/edu/bloom#ActionVerb> .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasCompetenceActivation
ontoksd:hasCompetenceActivation rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                                owl:inverseOf ontoksd:mediatesInstructionalUnit ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:InstructionalUnit ;
                                rdfs:range ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                                rdfs:comment """Associates an InstructionalUnit with a CompetenceActivation specifying how a particular competence is pedagogically addressed within that unit.

hasCompetenceActivation relates the instructional unit to the activation record; mediatesInstructionalUnit expresses the inverse direction. Each activation identifies exactly one instructional unit and exactly one competence, while an instructional unit may have multiple activation records.

The activation may specify pedagogical function, contribution, engagement modes, and applicable conditions. These qualifications belong to the association rather than being intrinsic properties of the instructional unit or the competence.

The association does not replace the unit's complete instructional description or establish that the planned work occurred, that requirements were satisfied, or that a learner demonstrated competence."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasCompetenceConstituent
ontoksd:hasCompetenceConstituent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isCompetenceConstituentOf ;
                                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                                 rdfs:range ontoksd:CompetenceConstituent ;
                                 rdfs:comment """Relates a Competence to a CompetenceConstituent that belongs to its internal semantic specification.

In OntoKSD, this property captures the fact that a competence is semantically structured by one or more constituent elements. These constituents may include knowledge, skill, disposition, or other specialized constituent forms defined in the ontology. The property provides the most general compositional relation between a competence and its internal semantic elements.

This relation should be used when the intention is to state that a constituent is part of the competence specification itself, rather than merely associated with a learner, an assessment event, or an instructional context.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasCompetenceScope
ontoksd:hasCompetenceScope rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                           rdfs:range ontoksd:CompetenceScope ;
                           rdfs:comment """Relates a Competence to a CompetenceScope that characterizes its broader domain or scope of applicability.

In OntoKSD, this property is used to indicate whether a competence is, for example, computing-specific, foundational, professional, transversal, or otherwise classified according to its intended scope. It supports semantic organization and analysis of competences across curricular and instructional contexts.

This property classifies the scope of the competence, not its internal structure or its specification pattern."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasComponentCompetence
ontoksd:hasComponentCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isComponentOfCompetence ;
                               rdf:type owl:AsymmetricProperty ,
                                        owl:IrreflexiveProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                               rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                               rdfs:comment """Relates a composite competence specification to a competence specification that directly contributes to its integrated expected performance.

In OntoKSD, hasComponentCompetence represents composition between individuals of Competence. It identifies direct component competences, which may themselves be atomic or composite. It is distinct from hasCompetenceConstituent, which relates a competence to knowledge, skill, disposition, or knowledge–performance specification elements.

Composition requires an intended integration of the component performances. Merely sharing knowledge, belonging to the same curriculum, or being addressed by the same instructional activity does not establish this relationship. The intended integration should be documented on the composite competence through hasIntegrationDescription.

The relation is irreflexive and asymmetric: a competence cannot directly contain itself, and two competences cannot directly contain each other. It is not declared transitive, preserving the distinction between direct and indirect components. Indirect components may be retrieved by traversing successive composition links. Longer composition cycles require separate query-based or validation checks.

A component competence remains independently identifiable and may participate in multiple composite specifications. The relation does not impose exclusive ownership or automatically transfer constituent assertions from components to the composite.

Under the class axioms adopted in OntoKSD, a competence with a component is classified as CompositeCompetence and is required to have at least two distinct component competences. The relation does not establish learner attainment: evidence of individual components does not automatically establish evidence of their integrated performance.

This property is the inverse of isComponentOfCompetence.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasContext
ontoksd:hasContext rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                   owl:inverseOf ontoksd:providesContextFor ;
                   rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:Competence
                                               ontoksd:CompetenceConstituent
                                               ontoksd:Evidence
                                               ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                               ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                             )
                               ] ;
                   rdfs:range ontoksd:Context ;
                   rdfs:comment """Relates a competence, competence constituent, evidence artifact, or evidenced competency element to the situational setting in which it is applicable, manifested, observed, interpreted, or evidenced.

In OntoKSD, hasContext is used to associate competence-related entities with a general Context that frames their relevance or interpretation. This context may correspond to professional, organizational, social, task-specific, or other situational conditions under which a competence or its related evidence becomes meaningful.

Unlike hasAcquisitionContext, which is restricted to pedagogically oriented settings of learning and assessment, hasContext captures the broader contextual conditions in which competencies or evidence are situated.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasCurricularKnowledgeReference
ontoksd:hasCurricularKnowledgeReference rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:KnowledgeSkill ;
                                        rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
                                        rdfs:comment """Relates a KnowledgeSkill to a curricular concept that explicitly anchors the knowledge component in a curricular framework.

In OntoKSD, this property is used to preserve explicit traceability between a KnowledgeSkill pairing and the curricular concept from which its knowledge component was derived or with which it is aligned. In CS2023- and CSP-aligned usage, the referenced concept is typically a Topic.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasDisposition
ontoksd:hasDisposition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasCompetenceConstituent ;
                       owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isDispositionOf ;
                       rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                       rdfs:range ontoksd:Disposition ;
                       rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence with a Disposition specified as part of its expected performance.

hasDisposition relates the competence to the dispositional constituent; isDispositionOf expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies an expected orientation influencing whether and how knowledge and skills are mobilized, rather than attributing a psychological characteristic to a learner.

A competence may include multiple dispositions, and a disposition specification may be reused across competences. Its relevance to the expected actions should remain explicit in each specification.

hasDisposition specializes hasCompetenceConstituent. The association does not establish that an individual possesses or has demonstrated the disposition; such interpretations require separately recorded evidence and judgments.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasDispositionCategory
ontoksd:hasDispositionCategory rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:Disposition ;
                               rdfs:range ontoksd:DispositionCategory .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasEvidence
ontoksd:hasEvidence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                    owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isEvidenceInProfile ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:Profile ;
                    rdfs:range ontoksd:Evidence ;
                    rdfs:comment """Associates a Profile with an Evidence instance included in the individual's educational record.

In OntoKSD, hasEvidence supports the organization and retrieval of artefacts or documented observations relevant to the profile owner. Inclusion does not imply that the individual produced the evidence, personally observed it, or is its exclusive subject. Shared evidence may be associated with multiple profiles where its relevance is documented.

Profile inclusion is distinct from evidential support for a particular judgment. That support is represented through supportedByEvidence on EvidencedCompetence or EvidencedCompetenceConstituent. An evidence instance included in a profile does not automatically support every judgment recorded there.

The association does not establish authenticity, validity, sufficiency, or competence attainment. It has domain Profile and range Evidence."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasEvidenceType
ontoksd:hasEvidenceType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:Evidence ;
                        rdfs:range ontoksd:EvidenceType ;
                        rdfs:comment """Relates an Evidence instance to an EvidenceType classifying its form or evidential nature.

The association may identify characteristics such as a written response, presentation recording, documented observation, simulation result, or technical report. Multiple compatible classifications may be assigned where their meanings are explicit.

Where types describe different dimensions, such as artefact form or reporting source, those dimensions should remain distinguishable. Classification does not identify the actual producer, observer, assessor, or assessment occurrence.

This property has domain Evidence and range EvidenceType. It does not establish authenticity, validity, reliability, sufficiency, or support for a particular judgment; that support is recorded separately through supportedByEvidence."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasEvidencedCompetence
ontoksd:hasEvidencedCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isEvidencedCompetenceOf ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:Profile ;
                               rdfs:range ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence ;
                               rdfs:comment """Associates a Profile with an EvidencedCompetence record concerning an evidence-based interpretation of its owner's performance.

hasEvidencedCompetence relates the profile to the record; isEvidencedCompetenceOf expresses the inverse direction. The profile owner must agree with the learner identified by the AssessmentParticipation grounding the record.

A profile may include multiple records concerning the same competence from different assessment occasions. Each record retains its supporting evidence, contextual qualifications, proficiency interpretation, and relevant dates. Inclusion does not automatically merge those records or select a current proficiency level.

The association organizes individual assessment records rather than linking the profile directly to a reusable Competence specification. It does not independently establish judgment validity, progression, complete mastery, or transfer across contexts.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasEvidencedConstituent
ontoksd:hasEvidencedConstituent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isEvidencedCompetenceConstituentOf ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence ;
                                rdfs:range ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent ;
                                rdfs:comment """Associates an EvidencedCompetence record with an EvidencedCompetenceConstituent record providing a constituent-level interpretation of the assessed performance.

hasEvidencedConstituent relates the whole-competence record to the constituent-level record; isEvidencedCompetenceConstituentOf expresses the inverse direction. The association connects assessment records, not their reusable competence specifications.

The records must concern the same learner and compatible assessment occasions. The constituent referenced by the finer-grained record must belong to the competence addressed by the whole-competence record. These correspondences require explicit verification.

Each record retains its own supporting evidence and applicable interpretation. Linking records does not automatically transfer evidence, aggregate proficiency levels, or establish that constituent demonstrations are sufficient for whole-competence attainment. For a CompositeCompetence, it does not establish integrated performance of its component competences.

The association supports traceability between assessment granularities without replacing the justification of either judgment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasInstructionalUnit
ontoksd:hasInstructionalUnit rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                             rdfs:domain ontoksd:Course ;
                             rdfs:range ontoksd:InstructionalUnit ;
                             rdfs:comment """Relates a Course to an InstructionalUnit included in its curricular organization.

In OntoKSD, hasInstructionalUnit associates a curricular component with planned learning activities, learning tasks, or assessments. It records instructional organization rather than an execution, a course offering, or learner participation.

A course may include multiple instructional units, and a unit may be associated with different courses where its specification remains applicable. Relevant differences in requirements or competence qualifications must remain explicit.

The association does not impose execution order, scheduling, or exclusive ownership. It does not automatically establish that the unit addresses every competence expected by the course or provides sufficient curricular coverage. Those correspondences require separately recorded competence associations and examination.

This property has domain Course and range InstructionalUnit.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasInterval
ontoksd:hasInterval rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                    owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isIntervalOf ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:Scale ;
                    rdfs:range ontoksd:ScaleInterval ;
                    rdfs:comment """Associates a Scale with a ScaleInterval whose numeric bounds are defined within that scale's range.

hasInterval relates the scale to the interval; isIntervalOf expresses the inverse direction. A scale may have multiple intervals, including alternative subdivisions adopted by different ProficiencyScheme instances.

The association identifies the numeric frame of reference. The interval's use within an interpretive scheme and its corresponding proficiency category are recorded separately through intervalDefinedInScheme and correspondsToLevel.

Intervals associated with the same scale do not necessarily form a single partition. Exhaustive coverage, non-overlap, valid boundaries, and consistency with the scale require explicit validation under the applicable scheme.

The association does not automatically classify scores, assign proficiency, or establish comparability between different interpretation schemes.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasKnowledge
ontoksd:hasKnowledge rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasCompetenceConstituent ;
                     owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isKnowledgeOf ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                     rdfs:range ontoksd:Knowledge ;
                     rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence directly with a Knowledge element included in its specification.

hasKnowledge relates the competence to its knowledge constituent; isKnowledgeOf expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies required knowledge content rather than asserting what an individual learner knows.

It is distinct from hasKnowledgeComponent, which identifies the knowledge within a KnowledgeSkill pairing. A knowledge element referenced through a pairing is not automatically asserted as directly linked through hasKnowledge.

hasKnowledge specializes hasCompetenceConstituent. The same knowledge element may be reused across competences. The association does not identify a required SkillLevel or establish knowledge acquisition or demonstration.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasKnowledgeComponent
ontoksd:hasKnowledgeComponent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:domain ontoksd:KnowledgeSkill ;
                              rdfs:range ontoksd:Knowledge ;
                              rdfs:comment """Relates a KnowledgeSkill pairing to the Knowledge element whose required performance level it specifies.

In OntoKSD, each KnowledgeSkill identifies exactly one Knowledge through hasKnowledgeComponent and exactly one required SkillLevel through hasSkillLevel. Together, these associations preserve which performance level applies to which knowledge content.

The same Knowledge element may participate in multiple pairings with different required levels. The level qualifies the requirement expressed by the pairing rather than an intrinsic characteristic of the knowledge.

This property is distinct from hasKnowledge, which directly associates a Competence with a Knowledge constituent. It has domain KnowledgeSkill and range Knowledge and does not establish learner knowledge, proficiency, or demonstrated performance."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasKnowledgeSkill
ontoksd:hasKnowledgeSkill rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasCompetenceConstituent ;
                          owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isKnowledgeSkillOf ;
                          rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                          rdfs:range ontoksd:KnowledgeSkill ;
                          rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence with a KnowledgeSkill pairing that specifies a required performance level for a particular knowledge element.

hasKnowledgeSkill relates the competence to the pairing; isKnowledgeSkillOf expresses the inverse direction. Each KnowledgeSkill identifies exactly one Knowledge through hasKnowledgeComponent and exactly one SkillLevel through hasSkillLevel.

The pairing preserves the correspondence between knowledge content and expected performance. Listing knowledge elements and skill levels independently would not establish which level applies to which knowledge. Multiple pairings therefore allow a competence to specify different performance requirements for different knowledge elements.

This representation supports the CC2020-oriented and CS2023-oriented specification patterns adopted in OntoKSD. The required level must be interpreted within its applicable reference scheme and satisfy the restrictions of the selected pattern.

hasKnowledgeSkill specializes hasCompetenceConstituent. A pairing is distinct from an explicitly identified Skill and does not imply that a SkillLevel is itself a skill. It may be reused across competence specifications only where its knowledge content and required level preserve their intended meaning.

The association belongs to the competence specification layer. It does not represent instructional activation, observed performance, or proficiency attributed to a learner, nor does it establish that the requirement has been satisfied.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasKnowledgeType
ontoksd:hasKnowledgeType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:Knowledge ;
                         rdfs:range ontoksd:KnowledgeType ;
                         rdfs:comment "Relates a Knowledge to its specific knowledge type."@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasLearner
ontoksd:hasLearner rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                   owl:inverseOf ontoksd:participatesIn ;
                   rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentParticipation ;
                   rdfs:range ontoksd:Learner ;
                   rdfs:comment """Identifies the Learner whose involvement is recorded by an AssessmentParticipation.

In OntoKSD, each AssessmentParticipation has exactly one learner. Combined with occursInAssessmentOccurrence, this association anchors participant-specific results and related evidential records to an identifiable learner and assessment occasion.

Learners participating in the same occurrence have separate participation records, even when they share an artefact or receive the same score. Identifying the learner does not automatically attribute all evidence from the occurrence to that individual or establish completion or competence attainment.

This property has domain AssessmentParticipation and range Learner and is the inverse of participatesIn.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasLearningNeed
ontoksd:hasLearningNeed rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                        owl:inverseOf ontoksd:identifiedIn ;
                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:Profile ;
                        rdfs:range ontoksd:LearningNeed ;
                        rdfs:comment "Lists the learning needs of a person."@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasPerformedRole
ontoksd:hasPerformedRole rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:Profile ;
                         rdfs:range ontoksd:RoleDetail ;
                         rdfs:comment "Indicates the role detail already performed by a person."@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasProficiencyLevel
ontoksd:hasProficiencyLevel rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            owl:inverseOf ontoksd:proficiencyLevelOf ;
                            rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                                        ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                                      )
                                        ] ;
                            rdfs:range ontoksd:ProficiencyLevel ;
                            rdfs:comment """Associates an EvidencedCompetence or EvidencedCompetenceConstituent record with the ProficiencyLevel assigned to its assessment interpretation.

hasProficiencyLevel relates the evidential record to the category; proficiencyLevelOf expresses the inverse direction. The category's meaning depends on an identifiable ProficiencyScheme and its applicable descriptors, criteria, or numeric interpretation rules.

The attributed level is distinct from an assessment score, a SkillLevel required by a competence specification, and a minimum proficiency expectation recorded for a course.

Each record may have at most one proficiency level under the adopted model. Separate records preserve interpretations from different occasions or under different schemes. Sharing a category does not identify the records or establish equivalent evidential bases.

The association records an interpretation rather than independently validating it. It does not establish complete mastery, progression, or transfer of performance across contexts.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasProfile
ontoksd:hasProfile rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                   owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isProfileOf ;
                   rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                   rdfs:domain ontoksd:Learner ;
                   rdfs:range ontoksd:Profile ;
                   rdfs:comment """Associates an individual with the Profile organizing that individual's educational and competence-related records.

hasProfile relates the individual to the profile; isProfileOf expresses the inverse direction. The profile is a separately identifiable record rather than the person, an assessment participation, or a competence specification.

Under the adopted single-profile model, each Learner has exactly one Profile, and each Profile identifies exactly one owner. The profile may organize multiple evidential records from different assessment occasions without merging their contexts, results, or supporting evidence.

The profile owner must agree with the learner identified by the participations grounding its competence-related records. The association alone does not verify this agreement.

Profile ownership does not establish that every included artefact was produced by the individual or that every recorded judgment is valid. It does not automatically diagnose learning needs, determine current proficiency, or establish progression.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasRCD
ontoksd:hasRCD rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
               owl:inverseOf ontoksd:representsCompetence ;
               rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
               rdfs:range ontoksd:OntoKSDRCD ;
               rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence specification with an RCD record representing it for identification, publication, and descriptive exchange.

hasRCD relates the competence to its documentary representation; representsCompetence expresses the inverse direction. The association preserves the distinction between the OntoKSD domain specification and the reusable definition record prepared according to an explicit mapping profile.

The profile determines which information is included, summarized, or referenced, including the specification pattern, constituents, knowledge–performance pairings, reference task, and structural relationships. The represented specification and its applicable revision must remain identifiable.

Where multiple RCD records represent the same competence, their purposes or revisions should be distinguishable. Record identifiers and metadata must remain consistent with the specification represented.

The association does not assert identity or semantic equivalence between the competence and its record. It does not automatically generate an export, preserve every OntoKSD axiom, establish IEEE conformance, or guarantee interoperability with a receiving system.

Learner-specific evidence, assessment results, and proficiency judgments are outside this definition-record association.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasResourceTypeConcept
ontoksd:hasResourceTypeConcept rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:EducationalResource ;
                               rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
                               rdfs:comment """Associates an EducationalResource with a controlled SKOS concept identifying its resource type.

In OntoKSD, hasResourceTypeConcept supports classification through concepts such as textbook, video, dataset, simulator, worksheet, or rubric. Each concept should belong to an identifiable scheme whose definitions guide consistent use.

A resource may have multiple compatible classifications. The association preserves the distinction between the educational artefact and the vocabulary concept used to classify it, without requiring every resource type to be modeled as an ontology subclass.

This property concerns resource classification rather than assessment classification, which is represented separately through hasAssessmentTypeConcept. It does not identify how a resource is used in a particular instructional unit; that association is recorded through usesResource and relevant instructional descriptions.

The property has domain EducationalResource and range skos:Concept. Its use does not, by itself, enforce membership in an approved scheme or establish pedagogical suitability, accessibility, quality, or contribution to competence attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasSkill
ontoksd:hasSkill rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasCompetenceConstituent ;
                 owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isSkillOf ;
                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                 rdfs:range ontoksd:Skill ;
                 rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence with an explicitly specified Skill constituent.

hasSkill relates the competence to the capability required by its specification; isSkillOf expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies expected ability rather than a learner's demonstrated capability.

A competence may include multiple skills, and the same skill may be reused across specifications. Associations between skills and relevant knowledge are represented separately through appliesKnowledge.

hasSkill specializes hasCompetenceConstituent. It does not identify a taxonomic performance level, imply a KnowledgeSkill pairing, or establish individual attainment."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasSkillDimension
ontoksd:hasSkillDimension rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:domain ontoksd:Skill ;
                          rdfs:range ontoksd:SkillDimension ;
                          rdfs:comment """Relates a Skill to a SkillDimension classifying an aspect of the capability it specifies.

In OntoKSD, hasSkillDimension supports organization and retrieval according to cognitive, technical, interpersonal, or other explicitly defined dimensions. Classification should follow the meaning of the skill description rather than its label alone.

A skill may have multiple compatible dimensions. Such assignments identify relevant aspects of the capability without imposing an exclusive primary dimension or ranking unless separately documented.

The association is distinct from a required SkillLevel, an attributed ProficiencyLevel, and an ActivationMode describing engagement within a particular instructional association.

This property has domain Skill and range SkillDimension. It classifies a specified capability rather than establishing that a learner possesses or has demonstrated it."""@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasSkillLevel
ontoksd:hasSkillLevel rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                      rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                      rdfs:domain ontoksd:KnowledgeSkill ;
                      rdfs:range <http://purl.org/edu/bloom#SkillLevel> ;
                      rdfs:comment """Relates a KnowledgeSkill pairing to the SkillLevel required for performance involving its associated Knowledge element.

In OntoKSD, each KnowledgeSkill identifies exactly one required level through hasSkillLevel and exactly one knowledge element through hasKnowledgeComponent. The level qualifies the knowledge-specific performance requirement rather than an intrinsic property of Knowledge or an explicitly identified Skill.

The applicable reference scheme must remain identifiable. Pairings used in CC2020Competence and CS2023Competence must satisfy the corresponding restrictions on CC2020SkillLevel and CS2023SkillLevel.

The same knowledge element may participate in different pairings with different required levels. A shared label or alignment with Bloom's taxonomy does not automatically make levels from different schemes identical or interchangeable.

This property has domain KnowledgeSkill and range SkillLevel. It expresses required performance, not an observed result, an attributed ProficiencyLevel, or evidence that a learner has satisfied the requirement.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasSpecialization
ontoksd:hasSpecialization rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isSpecializationOf ;
                          rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                          rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                          rdfs:comment """Relates a base competence specification to a competence specification that directly refines its performance scope.

In OntoKSD, hasSpecialization is the inverse of isSpecializationOf. If a competence C2 isSpecializationOf C1, then C1 hasSpecialization C2.

The relation identifies a directly linked specialization rather than a component competence, a prerequisite, or an arbitrary association between specifications. The specialized competence retains the central purpose of the base while introducing an explicitly documented refinement.

The relation is irreflexive, asymmetric, and not declared transitive. Indirect specializations may be retrieved by traversing successive links. The absence of specialization cycles longer than two links requires separate query-based or validation checks.

The explanation of the refinement is recorded on the specialized competence through hasSpecializationDescription and should identify the base specification concerned. A base competence may have multiple specializations, and a specialized competence may identify multiple bases where each relationship is explicitly justified.

The relation does not establish automatic inheritance of constituent assertions or imply that demonstrating a specialization automatically establishes learner attainment of its base.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasSpecificationPattern
ontoksd:hasSpecificationPattern rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                                rdfs:range ontoksd:SpecificationPattern ;
                                rdfs:comment """Relates a Competence to a SpecificationPattern that identifies how its internal semantic structure is specified.

In OntoKSD, this property is used to indicate the representational pattern adopted for the competence, such as formulations based on explicit Knowledge, Skill, and Disposition elements, or formulations based on KnowledgeSkill pairings and dispositions. It classifies the semantic style of specification used for the competence.

This property does not indicate whether the competence is atomic or composite. That distinction is captured separately through structural relations and structure classification.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasStructureType
ontoksd:hasStructureType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                         rdfs:range ontoksd:StructureType ;
                         skos:definition """Relates a Competence to a StructureType that classifies how it is structurally organized in relation to other competences.

In OntoKSD, this property is used to distinguish whether a competence is modeled as a singular specification unit or as a composite competence formed by other competences. It supports structural interpretation of the competence without determining the specific semantic pattern used for its internal constituent specification.

This property concerns inter-competence organization, not the particular constituent pattern adopted within the competence.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasSupportDocument
ontoksd:hasSupportDocument rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:Evidence ;
                           rdfs:range ontoksd:Document ;
                           rdfs:comment "Evidence can be supported by a Document"@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasTask
ontoksd:hasTask rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                owl:inverseOf ontoksd:isTaskOf ;
                rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                rdfs:range ontoksd:Task ;
                skos:definition """Relates a Competence to a Task that serves as a specification-level reference for the performance addressed by that competence.

In OntoKSD, a Task expresses what the competence is expected to enable, support, or orient in terms of purposeful performance. It is part of the semantic specification of the competence, rather than a contextual condition of activation or an instructional activity.

This property should not be used to represent pedagogical enactment. The associated Task is not an InstructionalUnit, LearningActivity, or LearningTask, but a specification-level construct that helps define the intended performance scope of the competence.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasTaskActivity
ontoksd:hasTaskActivity rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                        rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasTaskElement ;
                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:Task ;
                        rdfs:range ontoksd:TaskActivity ;
                        rdfs:comment """hasTaskActivity

Relates a Task to a TaskActivity that identifies the central action, operation, or expected form of engagement expressed in the task.

In OntoKSD, this property is used to make explicit the operative dimension of a task when its internal semantic structure is analyzed. In alignment with the CS2023 framework, the activity typically corresponds to the verb of the task statement and expresses what is to be done.

Typical values may correspond to actions such as develop, design, document, evaluate, maintain, improve, humanize, or research. For example, in a task such as “Develop a program for an open-ended problem”, develop denotes the task activity; in “Evaluate the efficiency of a parallel algorithm”, evaluate denotes the task activity.

This property is especially useful in contexts where task descriptions serve as bridges between textual analysis and competence specification, since it clarifies the kind of purposeful performance that the task requires.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasTaskComponent
ontoksd:hasTaskComponent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasTaskElement ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:Task ;
                         rdfs:range ontoksd:TaskComponent ;
                         rdfs:comment """hasTaskComponent

Relates a Task to a TaskComponent that identifies the object, artifact, domain entity, or semantic target involved in the task.

In OntoKSD, this property is used when a task is analytically decomposed in order to make explicit what the task is primarily about. In alignment with the CS2023 task-identification framework, the component often corresponds to the noun or noun phrase in the task statement and designates the referential focus toward which the task activity is directed.

Typical values may include entities such as a program, algorithm, system, architecture, dataset, platform, service, or representation. For example, in a task such as “Evaluate the efficiency of a parallel algorithm”, the algorithm functions as the principal task component.

This property supports clearer semantic anchoring of the task in relation to domain concepts and helps connect task wording to competence specification.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasTaskConstraint
ontoksd:hasTaskConstraint rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:hasTaskElement ;
                          rdfs:domain ontoksd:Task ;
                          rdfs:range ontoksd:TaskConstraint ;
                          rdfs:comment """hasTaskConstraint

Relates a Task to a TaskConstraint that identifies a delimiting condition, requirement, limitation, or qualifying circumstance associated with the task.

In OntoKSD, this property is used to make explicit how a task is bounded, qualified, or contextually specified. In alignment with the CS2023 framework, constraints may be expressed through adjectives, adverbs, or qualifying phrases in the task statement, and may concern the problem, the expected solution, or implementation conditions.

Typical values may include conditions such as open-ended, efficient, secure, scalable, reliable, parallel, distributed, low-cost, or team-based. For example, in “Develop a program for an open-ended problem”, open-ended functions as a task constraint; in “Evaluate the efficiency of a parallel algorithm”, efficiency and parallel express qualifying conditions that shape the intended interpretation of the task.

This property is especially valuable for preserving semantic precision, since it helps distinguish the core action and target of the task from the conditions that delimit how the task is to be understood or performed.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasTaskElement
ontoksd:hasTaskElement rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:domain ontoksd:Task ;
                       rdfs:range ontoksd:TaskElement ;
                       rdfs:comment """hasTaskElement

Relates a Task to a TaskElement that represents an analytically distinguishable part of its internal semantic structure.

In OntoKSD, this property is used to support the optional decomposition of a specification-level Task into more explicit semantic dimensions, especially when task descriptions are analyzed according to the CS2023 framework for systematically identifying tasks or within the Competency Specification Process.

The property provides a general relation through which more specific dimensions of task analysis, such as component, activity, and constraint, may be represented. In this sense, it enables OntoKSD to preserve traceability between the original wording of a task statement and its more structured semantic interpretation.

This property should be understood as a descriptive relation internal to Task analysis. It does not denote a relation between a task and a competence, nor a part-whole relation between instructional units.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#identifiedIn
ontoksd:identifiedIn rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:LearningNeed ;
                     rdfs:range ontoksd:Profile .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#interpretedUsingScheme
ontoksd:interpretedUsingScheme rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence ;
                               rdfs:range ontoksd:ProficiencyScheme ;
                               rdfs:comment """Relates an EvidencedCompetence or EvidencedCompetenceConstituent record to the ProficiencyScheme governing its proficiency interpretation.

In OntoKSD, interpretedUsingSchema identifies the scheme whose descriptors, criteria, or numeric interval rules provide meaning to the record's attributed ProficiencyLevel. It preserves interpretive traceability when different records within the same assessment occurrence use different schemes.

The attributed level must be defined within the identified scheme. Where interpretation uses a numeric result, the relevant score, scale, and interval correspondence should remain identifiable and consistent.

The association is distinct from usesProficiencyScheme on AssessmentOccurrence, which identifies a scheme at the occurrence level. The scheme governing each individual interpretation must remain unambiguous.

This property has domain the union of EvidencedCompetence and EvidencedCompetenceConstituent and range ProficiencyScheme. It documents the interpretive basis without automatically classifying results, validating judgments, or establishing competence attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#intervalDefinedInScheme
ontoksd:intervalDefinedInScheme rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:ScaleInterval ;
                                rdfs:range ontoksd:ProficiencyScheme ;
                                rdfs:comment """Associates a ScaleInterval with the ProficiencyScheme in which it is adopted for numeric interpretation.

intervalDefinedInScheme relates the interval to the scheme; definesInterval expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies the interpretive structure governing the interval's use and its correspondence to a ProficiencyLevel.

The interval's associated Scale and proficiency category must be consistent with the identified scheme. The same scale may support different schemes with different subdivisions or category meanings. Where identical boundaries have different interpretations, separate interval specifications should preserve those distinctions.

Qualitative schemes need not define numeric intervals. This association does not, by itself, verify coverage, overlaps, gaps, or boundary consistency, nor does it classify a score or assign learner proficiency.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#involvesAssessmentParticipation
ontoksd:involvesAssessmentParticipation rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        owl:inverseOf ontoksd:occursInAssessmentOccurrence ;
                                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                                        rdfs:range ontoksd:AssessmentParticipation ;
                                        rdfs:comment """Relates an AssessmentOccurrence to an AssessmentParticipation recording an individual learner's involvement in that evaluative event.

In OntoKSD, an occurrence may involve multiple participation records, each identifying exactly one learner and referring to exactly one occurrence. Assessors, individual scores, and links from competence-related evidential records may be associated with each participation.

The relation supports both individual and group-based assessment. Learners may share an occurrence or artefact without sharing identical scores, supporting evidence, or judgments.

Linking a participation to an occurrence does not, by itself, establish attendance throughout the event, completion of the work, or competence attainment.

This property has domain AssessmentOccurrence and range AssessmentParticipation and is the inverse of occursInAssessmentOccurrence.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isAcquisitionContextOf
ontoksd:isAcquisitionContextOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:AcquisitionContext ;
                               rdfs:range ontoksd:InstructionalUnit .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isActivationFunctionOf
ontoksd:isActivationFunctionOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:ActivationFunction ;
                               rdfs:range ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                               rdfs:comment """Associates a CompetenceActivation with an ActivationFunction identifying the pedagogical purpose of the competence–instructional unit association.

hasActivationFunction relates the activation to the function value; isActivationFunctionOf expresses the inverse direction. Examples include addressing a competence as an instructional target or presupposing it as a prerequisite, where these distinctions are explicitly adopted.

Function identifies pedagogical purpose rather than the competence's contribution, form of engagement, or applicable conditions, which are represented through role, mode, and constraint qualifications.

Function values are reusable classifications. The same value may qualify multiple activations without identifying those associations as the same entity. Multiple assignments require a coherent interpretation in the instructional specification.

The association records an educational intention or presupposition. It does not establish that instruction occurred, that a learner satisfies a prerequisite, or that competence was attained.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isActivationQualifierOf
ontoksd:isActivationQualifierOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:ActivationQualifier ;
                                rdfs:range ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                                rdfs:comment """Associates a CompetenceActivation with an ActivationQualifier describing the competence's contribution, expected engagement, or applicable conditions within an instructional unit.

hasActivationQualifier relates the activation to its qualifier; isActivationQualifierOf expresses the inverse direction. Specialized associations are represented through hasActivationRole, hasActivationMode, and hasActivationConstraint.

An activation may have multiple qualifiers. Shared values or constraint specifications do not identify distinct activations as the same entity. ActivationFunction is associated separately through hasActivationFunction.

The association qualifies planned instructional use without modifying the competence definition or establishing that the expected performance occurred.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isAttitudeOf
ontoksd:isAttitudeOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:isDispositionOf ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:Attitude ;
                     rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                     rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence with an Attitude specified as an evaluative orientation relevant to its expected performance.

hasAttitude relates the competence to the attitudinal constituent; isAttitudeOf expresses the inverse direction. The attitude identifies an expected position toward a relevant object, practice, behavior, or situation.

Because Attitude specializes Disposition, hasAttitude specializes hasDisposition, and isAttitudeOf specializes isDispositionOf. An attitudinal association therefore also constitutes a dispositional association. The reverse implication does not hold: a generic disposition does not automatically satisfy an attitude requirement.

The association supports explicit attitudinal requirements, including those of the KSA specification pattern. It does not attribute an attitude to a learner or establish its manifestation, stability, or transfer across contexts.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isBasedOnActivity
ontoksd:isBasedOnActivity rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:domain ontoksd:Assessment ;
                          rdfs:range ontoksd:LearningActivity ;
                          rdfs:comment """Relates an Assessment specification to a LearningActivity whose expected work, products, or engagement provide a basis for its evaluative design.

In OntoKSD, isBasedOnActivity connects learning-oriented planning with a separately identifiable assessment specification. The referenced activity may be a LearningTask, and an assessment may draw on multiple activities where their contributions are explicitly described.

The association does not identify the activity with the assessment or imply that every aspect of the activity is evaluated. The expected evidence and applicable criteria should make clear which aspects inform judgment.

This property has domain Assessment and range LearningActivity. It concerns specifications rather than execution events and does not establish that the activity occurred, evidence was collected, or competence was demonstrated.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isCompetenceConstituentOf
ontoksd:isCompetenceConstituentOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                  rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceConstituent ;
                                  rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                                  rdfs:comment """Associates a CompetenceConstituent with a Competence whose semantic specification includes that element.

isCompetenceConstituentOf relates the constituent to the competence; hasCompetenceConstituent expresses the inverse direction. Specialized relations identify Knowledge, Skill, Disposition, including Attitude, and KnowledgeSkill constituents while supporting their uniform retrieval.

A constituent may participate in multiple competence specifications where its meaning remains applicable. The association does not imply exclusive ownership, identity between constituent and competence, or automatic transfer of learner-specific evidence.

The relation expresses inclusion in a semantic specification rather than gUFO object-level component parthood. It is distinct from composition between competences and from the reference-task association represented through hasTask and isTaskOf.

The association does not, by itself, establish a complete specification, satisfy all requirements of an adopted pattern, or demonstrate learner attainment. Its domain is CompetenceConstituent and its range is Competence.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isComponentOfCompetence
ontoksd:isComponentOfCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                                rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                                rdfs:comment """Relates a component competence specification to a composite competence specification in whose integrated expected performance it directly participates.

In OntoKSD, isComponentOfCompetence is the inverse of hasComponentCompetence. If a competence C1 hasComponentCompetence C2, then C2 isComponentOfCompetence C1.

The relation expresses direct participation in competence composition rather than specialization, shared subject matter, or association with the same instructional activity. The contribution of the component to the integrated performance should be explained through hasIntegrationDescription on the composite competence.

A component may be atomic or composite and may contribute to more than one composite specification. Being a component does not alter its independently identifiable definition or imply exclusive ownership by a composite.

The relation is irreflexive, asymmetric, and not declared transitive. Successive links may be traversed to retrieve indirect containing competences, while longer composition cycles require separate query-based or validation checks.

This relation concerns the organization of competence specifications. It does not assert that a learner has demonstrated either the component competence or its integration within the composite.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isConstituentEvidencedBy
ontoksd:isConstituentEvidencedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 owl:inverseOf ontoksd:refersToCompetenceConstituent ;
                                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceConstituent ;
                                 rdfs:range ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isContextOfAssessmentOccurrence
ontoksd:isContextOfAssessmentOccurrence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        owl:inverseOf ontoksd:occursInAcquisitionContext ;
                                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:AcquisitionContext ;
                                        rdfs:range ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                                        rdfs:comment """Associates an AssessmentOccurrence with the AcquisitionContext describing the educational circumstances of that evaluative event.

occursInAcquisitionContext relates the occurrence to its context; isContextOfAssessmentOccurrence expresses the inverse direction. The occurrence represents the event, while the context describes its relevant configuration of resources, collaboration arrangements, environmental conditions, or other educational circumstances.

The recorded circumstances may differ from those anticipated by the Assessment specification. Such differences should remain explicit rather than silently replacing the intended context.

The association does not identify the event with its context or establish that instructional requirements were satisfied, that all participants experienced identical conditions, or that competence was attained.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isCurricularlyRepresentedBy
ontoksd:isCurricularlyRepresentedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:Knowledge ;
                                    rdfs:range skos:Concept .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isDispositionOf
ontoksd:isDispositionOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                        rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:isCompetenceConstituentOf ;
                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:Disposition ;
                        rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                        rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence with a Disposition specified as part of its expected performance.

hasDisposition relates the competence to the dispositional constituent; isDispositionOf expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies an expected orientation influencing whether and how knowledge and skills are mobilized, rather than attributing a psychological characteristic to a learner.

A competence may include multiple dispositions, and a disposition specification may be reused across competences. Its relevance to the expected actions should remain explicit in each specification.

hasDisposition specializes hasCompetenceConstituent. The association does not establish that an individual possesses or has demonstrated the disposition; such interpretations require separately recorded evidence and judgments.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isEvidenceInProfile
ontoksd:isEvidenceInProfile rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            rdfs:domain ontoksd:Evidence ;
                            rdfs:range ontoksd:Profile .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isEvidencedBy
ontoksd:isEvidencedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                      owl:inverseOf ontoksd:refersToCompetence ;
                      rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                      rdfs:range ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isEvidencedCompetenceConstituentOf
ontoksd:isEvidencedCompetenceConstituentOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent ;
                                           rdfs:range ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isEvidencedCompetenceOf
ontoksd:isEvidencedCompetenceOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence ;
                                rdfs:range ontoksd:Profile .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isEvidencedInAssessmentOccurrence
ontoksd:isEvidencedInAssessmentOccurrence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                          rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                                                      ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                                                    )
                                                      ] ;
                                          rdfs:range ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                                          rdfs:comment """isEvidencedInAssessmentOccurrence links an EvidencedCompetence or an EvidencedCompetenceConstituent to the particular AssessmentOccurrence in which that evidential record is produced, recognized, or interpreted. Its purpose is to make explicit the event-level anchoring of competence evidence in OntoKSD.

This property reinforces the distinction between abstract competence specifications and their contextualized manifestations. While Competence represents a relatively stable and reusable semantic construct, EvidencedCompetence and EvidencedCompetenceConstituent represent situated records associated with a particular learner participation and a concrete assessment event. By explicitly relating such records to an AssessmentOccurrence, OntoKSD captures the episodic nature of competence evidence and supports the interpretation that competence manifestations are tied to a specific subject, moment, task context, and evaluative setting.

In the ontology, this property complements the relation derivedFromParticipation, since the corresponding AssessmentOccurrence may also be recovered through the AssessmentParticipation from which the evidenced record derives. Its explicit inclusion improves semantic clarity, traceability, and query simplicity, especially in scenarios where event-centered analysis of competence evidence is required.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isIntervalOf
ontoksd:isIntervalOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:ScaleInterval ;
                     rdfs:range ontoksd:Scale .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isKnowledgeOf
ontoksd:isKnowledgeOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                      rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:isCompetenceConstituentOf ;
                      rdfs:domain ontoksd:Knowledge ;
                      rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                      rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence directly with a Knowledge element included in its specification.

hasKnowledge relates the competence to its knowledge constituent; isKnowledgeOf expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies required knowledge content rather than asserting what an individual learner knows.

It is distinct from hasKnowledgeComponent, which identifies the knowledge within a KnowledgeSkill pairing. A knowledge element referenced through a pairing is not automatically asserted as directly linked through hasKnowledge.

hasKnowledge specializes hasCompetenceConstituent. The same knowledge element may be reused across competences. The association does not identify a required SkillLevel or establish knowledge acquisition or demonstration.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isKnowledgeSkillOf
ontoksd:isKnowledgeSkillOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:isCompetenceConstituentOf ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:KnowledgeSkill ;
                           rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                           rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence with a KnowledgeSkill pairing that specifies a required performance level for a particular knowledge element.

hasKnowledgeSkill relates the competence to the pairing; isKnowledgeSkillOf expresses the inverse direction. Each KnowledgeSkill identifies exactly one Knowledge through hasKnowledgeComponent and exactly one SkillLevel through hasSkillLevel.

The pairing preserves the correspondence between knowledge content and expected performance. Listing knowledge elements and skill levels independently would not establish which level applies to which knowledge. Multiple pairings therefore allow a competence to specify different performance requirements for different knowledge elements.

This representation supports the CC2020-oriented and CS2023-oriented specification patterns adopted in OntoKSD. The required level must be interpreted within its applicable reference scheme and satisfy the restrictions of the selected pattern.

hasKnowledgeSkill specializes hasCompetenceConstituent. A pairing is distinct from an explicitly identified Skill and does not imply that a SkillLevel is itself a skill. It may be reused across competence specifications only where its knowledge content and required level preserve their intended meaning.

The association belongs to the competence specification layer. It does not represent instructional activation, observed performance, or proficiency attributed to a learner, nor does it establish that the requirement has been satisfied.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isProfileOf
ontoksd:isProfileOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ,
                             owl:InverseFunctionalProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:Profile ;
                    rdfs:range ontoksd:Learner .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isRealizedBy
ontoksd:isRealizedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                     owl:inverseOf ontoksd:realizes ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:Assessment ;
                     rdfs:range ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isSkillOf
ontoksd:isSkillOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                  rdfs:subPropertyOf ontoksd:isCompetenceConstituentOf ;
                  rdfs:domain ontoksd:Skill ;
                  rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                  rdfs:comment """Associates a Competence with an explicitly specified Skill constituent.

hasSkill relates the competence to the capability required by its specification; isSkillOf expresses the inverse direction. The association identifies expected ability rather than a learner's demonstrated capability.

A competence may include multiple skills, and the same skill may be reused across specifications. Associations between skills and relevant knowledge are represented separately through appliesKnowledge.

hasSkill specializes hasCompetenceConstituent. It does not identify a taxonomic performance level, imply a KnowledgeSkill pairing, or establish individual attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isSpecializationOf
ontoksd:isSpecializationOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ,
                                    owl:AsymmetricProperty ,
                                    owl:IrreflexiveProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                           rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                           rdfs:comment """Comentário para lembrar o sparql de competências envolvidas em ciclos:

SELECT DISTINCT ?competence
WHERE {
  ?competence
    (ontoksd:isSpecializationOf|^ontoksd:hasSpecialization)+
    ?competence .
}""" ,
                                        """Relates a competence specification to an explicitly identified base competence specification whose performance scope it directly refines.

In OntoKSD, isSpecializationOf expresses a declared specialization between individuals of Competence. The specialized specification preserves the central purpose of its base while introducing a narrower scope or additional delimiting conditions. The refinement may concern the domain of application, the class of problems addressed, the permitted techniques, or other explicitly described performance conditions.

The relation represents direct specialization within the adopted specification structure. It is not declared transitive: successive specialization links may be traversed to retrieve indirect bases without treating them as directly asserted relationships. Directness is a modeling convention and is not established merely by omitting a transitivity axiom.

The relation is irreflexive and asymmetric. A competence cannot specialize itself, and two competences cannot directly specialize each other. Longer specialization cycles must be checked separately through queries or validation.

The narrower scope and its relationship to the base specification should be documented through hasSpecializationDescription. Shared knowledge, participation in the same activity, or a higher required skill level does not, by itself, establish specialization.

This relation does not automatically copy constituent assertions from the base specification, establish competence composition, or attribute attainment to a learner. It is the inverse of hasSpecialization.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isTaskOf
ontoksd:isTaskOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:Task ;
                 rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#levelDefinedInScheme
ontoksd:levelDefinedInScheme rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                             rdfs:domain ontoksd:ProficiencyLevel ;
                             rdfs:range ontoksd:ProficiencyScheme .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#mediatesCompetence
ontoksd:mediatesCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates> ;
                           rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                           rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                           rdfs:comment """Relates a CompetenceActivation to the Competence specification addressed by its instructional association.

In OntoKSD, each CompetenceActivation identifies exactly one competence through mediatesCompetence and exactly one instructional unit through mediatesInstructionalUnit. The association may be qualified by pedagogical function, contribution, expected engagement modes, and applicable conditions.

The property does not itself classify the competence as a prerequisite. Where prerequisiteFunction is assigned through hasActivationFunction, the activation records that the competence is presupposed for engagement in the instructional unit; it does not establish that a learner satisfies that expectation.

The same competence may participate in multiple activations with different instructional qualifications while retaining its reusable definition. Changes in qualification must not silently alter its constituent requirements or expected performance.

This property has domain CompetenceActivation and range Competence. It does not express a dependency between competence specifications, identify learner-specific attainment, or establish that the planned mobilization occurred.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#mediatesCourse
ontoksd:mediatesCourse rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates> ;
                       rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                       rdfs:domain ontoksd:CourseCompetenceSpecification ;
                       rdfs:range ontoksd:Course ;
                       rdfs:comment """mediatesCourse
Relates a CourseCompetenceSpecification to the Course whose curricular scope it qualifies with respect to a given competence.

In OntoKSD, mediatesCourse is used to indicate that a CourseCompetenceSpecification semantically involves a particular course as one of the relata of the curricular specification. Through this relation, the ontology makes explicit that the specification is not an abstract statement about competence alone, but a qualified curricular association anchored in a specific Course.

This property should be interpreted together with mediatesCourseCompetence, since both relations jointly identify the two poles connected by the same curricular specification.

Ontological rationale:
mediatesCourse is modeled as a mediation relation because CourseCompetenceSpecification reifies the qualified association between a course and a competence. The property makes explicit the participation of the course in that relator, rather than reducing the association to a direct unqualified link.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#mediatesCourseCompetence
ontoksd:mediatesCourseCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates> ;
                                 rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:CourseCompetenceSpecification ;
                                 rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                                 rdfs:comment """mediatesCourseCompetence
Relates a CourseCompetenceSpecification to the Competence that is curricularly specified in association with a given Course.

In OntoKSD, mediatesCourseCompetence is used to indicate that a CourseCompetenceSpecification semantically involves a particular competence as one of the relata of the curricular specification. Through this relation, the ontology makes explicit which competence is included, expected, or required within the curricular scope of the course.

This property should be interpreted together with mediatesCourse, since both relations jointly represent the qualified association reified by the same CourseCompetenceSpecification.

Ontological rationale:
mediatesCourseCompetence is modeled as a mediation relation because the association between a course and a competence is treated in OntoKSD as a semantically qualified curricular specification. The property identifies the competence involved in that relator while preserving the possibility of attaching additional constraints and qualifications to the association.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#mediatesExternalCompetence
ontoksd:mediatesExternalCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates> ;
                                   rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                   rdfs:domain ontoksd:ExternalCompetenceAlignment ;
                                   rdfs:range ontoksd:ExternalCompetence ;
                                   rdfs:label "mediates external competence"@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#mediatesInstructionalUnit
ontoksd:mediatesInstructionalUnit rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates> ;
                                  rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                  rdfs:domain ontoksd:CompetenceActivation ;
                                  rdfs:range ontoksd:InstructionalUnit ;
                                  rdfs:comment """Associates an InstructionalUnit with a CompetenceActivation specifying how a particular competence is pedagogically addressed within that unit.

hasCompetenceActivation relates the instructional unit to the activation record; mediatesInstructionalUnit expresses the inverse direction. Each activation identifies exactly one instructional unit and exactly one competence, while an instructional unit may have multiple activation records.

The activation may specify pedagogical function, contribution, engagement modes, and applicable conditions. These qualifications belong to the association rather than being intrinsic properties of the instructional unit or the competence.

The association does not replace the unit's complete instructional description or establish that the planned work occurred, that requirements were satisfied, or that a learner demonstrated competence.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#mediatesInternalCompetence
ontoksd:mediatesInternalCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates> ;
                                   rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                   rdfs:domain ontoksd:ExternalCompetenceAlignment ;
                                   rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                                   rdfs:label "mediates internal competence"@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#occursInAcquisitionContext
ontoksd:occursInAcquisitionContext rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                   rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                                   rdfs:range ontoksd:AcquisitionContext ;
                                   rdfs:comment """Associates an AssessmentOccurrence with the AcquisitionContext describing the educational circumstances of that evaluative event.

occursInAcquisitionContext relates the occurrence to its context; isContextOfAssessmentOccurrence expresses the inverse direction. The occurrence represents the event, while the context describes its relevant configuration of resources, collaboration arrangements, environmental conditions, or other educational circumstances.

The recorded circumstances may differ from those anticipated by the Assessment specification. Such differences should remain explicit rather than silently replacing the intended context.

The association does not identify the event with its context or establish that instructional requirements were satisfied, that all participants experienced identical conditions, or that competence was attained.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#occursInAssessmentOccurrence
ontoksd:occursInAssessmentOccurrence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentParticipation ;
                                     rdfs:range ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                                     rdfs:comment """Relates an AssessmentParticipation to the AssessmentOccurrence in which the learner's recorded participation takes place.

In OntoKSD, each AssessmentParticipation refers to exactly one occurrence. This association anchors participant-specific results and related evidential interpretations to an identifiable assessment occasion. Participation in another occurrence is represented by a separate record.

The relation does not, by itself, define a uniqueness key for participation records or establish attendance throughout the event, completion, or competence attainment. It links a participation record to an event without asserting gUFO mediation.

This property has domain AssessmentParticipation and range AssessmentOccurrence and is the inverse of involvesAssessmentParticipation.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#participatesIn
ontoksd:participatesIn rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:domain ontoksd:Learner ;
                       rdfs:range ontoksd:AssessmentParticipation ;
                       rdfs:comment "Relates a Learner to an AssessmentParticipation that records that learner's involvement in a particular assessment occurrence. This property is the inverse of hasLearner; it does not directly relate the learner to the event." .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#producesEvidence
ontoksd:producesEvidence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                         rdfs:range ontoksd:Evidence ;
                         rdfs:comment """Relates an AssessmentOccurrence to an Evidence instance produced during that concrete evaluative event.

In OntoKSD, producesEvidence records the occurrence-level origin of an evidential artefact or documented observation. The evidence may concern individual or collective work, but its association with the occurrence does not automatically attribute it to every participant or establish an identical evidential basis for their judgments.

The evidence supporting a particular competence-related judgment is identified separately through supportedByEvidence on EvidencedCompetence or EvidencedCompetenceConstituent. Production of evidence does not, by itself, establish its adequacy, validation, or support for competence attainment.

When an assessment examines an artefact produced earlier, its use in that assessment must remain distinguishable from its original production. A new observation or evaluative record concerning that artefact may be produced during the occurrence without implying that the artefact itself originated there.

This property has domain AssessmentOccurrence and range Evidence and is the inverse of evidenceBasedOn.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#proficiencyLevelOf
ontoksd:proficiencyLevelOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:ProficiencyLevel ;
                           rdfs:range [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                                      ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                                    )
                                      ] ;
                           rdfs:comment """Relates a ProficiencyLevel to the EvidencedCompetence or EvidencedCompetenceConstituent to which that level is attributed.

In OntoKSD, proficiencyLevelOf is used to represent that a contextualized evidential record has been interpreted or classified according to a proficiency level. This property supports the attribution of proficiency to demonstrated competence records rather than to abstract competency specifications.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#providesContextFor
ontoksd:providesContextFor rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:Context ;
                           rdfs:range [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:Competence
                                                      ontoksd:CompetenceConstituent
                                                      ontoksd:Evidence
                                                      ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                                      ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                                    )
                                      ] .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#providesEvidence
ontoksd:providesEvidence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:RoleDetail ;
                         rdfs:range ontoksd:Evidence ;
                         rdfs:comment "Specifies the evidence provided in a role detail."@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#providesSelfAssessment
ontoksd:providesSelfAssessment rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain ontoksd:Profile ;
                               rdfs:range ontoksd:Evidence ;
                               rdfs:comment "Links a person to a self-assessment evidence."@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#realizes
ontoksd:realizes rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                 rdfs:range ontoksd:Assessment ;
                 rdfs:comment """Relates an AssessmentOccurrence to the Assessment specification carried out in that concrete evaluative event.

In OntoKSD, realizes links evaluative execution to its pedagogical specification. Each AssessmentOccurrence realizes exactly one Assessment, while the same Assessment may be realized on multiple occasions with different participants and contextual conditions.

The relation identifies the specification governing the occurrence. It does not, by itself, establish that every planned procedure was followed, every criterion was applied, or every participant completed the assessment or demonstrated competence. Relevant deviations from the specification should be documented separately.

This property has domain AssessmentOccurrence and range Assessment and is the inverse of isRealizedBy.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#referencesEvidencedCompetence
ontoksd:referencesEvidencedCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                      rdfs:domain ontoksd:Document ;
                                      rdfs:range ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence ;
                                      rdfs:comment """Relates a Document to an EvidencedCompetence record that it identifies or discusses.

In OntoKSD, referencesEvidencedCompetence supports traceability between documentary artefacts, such as reports, portfolios, or certificates, and contextualized competence-related judgments. A document may reference multiple records, and a record may be referenced by multiple documents.

Documentary reference is distinct from evidential support. The association does not automatically classify the document as Evidence or establish that it substantiates, validates, or certifies the referenced judgment. Supporting evidence is identified separately through supportedByEvidence.

This property has domain Document and range EvidencedCompetence. It references a learner-specific record rather than the reusable Competence specification and does not establish current proficiency or competence attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#referencesEvidencedCompetenceConstituent
ontoksd:referencesEvidencedCompetenceConstituent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:Document ;
                                                 rdfs:range ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent ;
                                                 rdfs:comment """Relates a Document to an EvidencedCompetenceConstituent record that it identifies or discusses.

In OntoKSD, referencesEvidencedCompetenceConstituent supports traceability between documentary artefacts and contextualized constituent-level judgments. A document may reference multiple records, and a record may be referenced by multiple documents.

The association concerns the assessment record rather than the reusable CompetenceConstituent specification. It does not automatically classify the document as Evidence or establish evidential support, validation, or certification of the judgment. Supporting evidence is identified separately through supportedByEvidence.

This property has domain Document and range EvidencedCompetenceConstituent. A reference to a constituent-level record does not establish attainment of the encompassing competence or integration of its components.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#refersToCompetence
ontoksd:refersToCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence ;
                           rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                           rdfs:comment """Associates an EvidencedCompetence record with the Competence specification addressed by its assessment interpretation.

refersToCompetence relates the learner-specific record to the reusable specification; isEvidencedBy expresses the inverse direction. Each record identifies exactly one competence, while the same competence may be referenced by multiple records concerning different learners, occasions, or interpretations.

The association identifies the target of the judgment rather than its supporting evidence. Evidence, participation, applicable criteria, proficiency interpretation, and relevant dates are recorded separately and must remain consistent with the referenced specification.

Despite its name, isEvidencedBy relates a Competence to an EvidencedCompetence record, not directly to an Evidence instance. The distinction preserves the separation between expected performance, its assessment interpretation, and the material supporting that interpretation.

The association does not modify the competence definition or independently establish complete mastery, judgment validity, progression, or transfer across contexts.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#refersToCompetenceConstituent
ontoksd:refersToCompetenceConstituent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                      rdfs:domain ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent ;
                                      rdfs:range ontoksd:CompetenceConstituent ;
                                      rdfs:comment """Associates an EvidencedCompetenceConstituent record with the CompetenceConstituent addressed by its assessment interpretation.

refersToCompetenceConstituent relates the contextualized record to the reusable constituent specification; isConstituentEvidencedBy expresses the inverse direction. Each record identifies exactly one constituent, which may be Knowledge, Skill, Disposition, including Attitude, or KnowledgeSkill.

The association identifies the target of the judgment rather than its supporting evidence, learner, or assessment occasion. Those elements are represented through separate relations.

The same constituent may be referenced by multiple records concerning different learners, occasions, or interpretations. Where a record is linked to an EvidencedCompetence, its referenced constituent must be consistent with the competence addressed by that whole-competence record.

The association does not modify the constituent specification or independently establish mastery, judgment validity, or attainment of an encompassing competence.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#refersToRole
ontoksd:refersToRole rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:RoleDetail ;
                     rdfs:range ontoksd:Learner ;
                     rdfs:comment "Links a role detail to a specific role."@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#representsCompetence
ontoksd:representsCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                             rdfs:domain ontoksd:OntoKSDRCD ;
                             rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#representsKnowledgeArea
ontoksd:representsKnowledgeArea rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                rdfs:domain ontoksd:Knowledge ;
                                rdfs:range skos:Concept .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#requiresMinimumProficiencyLevel
ontoksd:requiresMinimumProficiencyLevel rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:CourseCompetenceSpecification ;
                                        rdfs:range ontoksd:ProficiencyLevel ;
                                        rdfs:comment """Relates a CourseCompetenceSpecification to the minimum ProficiencyLevel that the course is intended to address for its associated competence.

In OntoKSD, this property qualifies a curricular expectation rather than an individual assessment result. It expresses the intended depth of performance beyond merely listing the competence within the course.

The applicable ProficiencyScheme must remain identifiable. Interpreting the value as a minimum requires a documented ordering or comparison rule within that scheme; category labels or ordinal positions alone do not establish comparability across schemes.

Each CourseCompetenceSpecification may identify at most one minimum level under the adopted model. Different courses may set different expectations for the same reusable Competence without changing its definition.

The expected level is distinct from a SkillLevel within a KnowledgeSkill pairing, a numeric passing score, an admission prerequisite, and proficiency attributed to a learner.

This property has domain CourseCompetenceSpecification and range ProficiencyLevel. Its assertion records a curricular commitment; it does not establish sufficient instructional coverage, fulfillment of that commitment, course approval, or learner attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#supportedByEvidence
ontoksd:supportedByEvidence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                                        ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                                      )
                                        ] ;
                            rdfs:range ontoksd:Evidence .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#targetsCompetence
ontoksd:targetsCompetence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                          rdfs:domain ontoksd:LearningNeed ;
                          rdfs:range ontoksd:Competence ;
                          rdfs:comment "Defines the competence needed by a learning need."@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#targetsCompetenceConstituent
ontoksd:targetsCompetenceConstituent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:LearningNeed ;
                                     rdfs:range ontoksd:CompetenceConstituent ;
                                     rdfs:comment "Defines the competency required by a learning need."@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#usedAsTypeOfKnowledge
ontoksd:usedAsTypeOfKnowledge rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:domain skos:Concept ;
                              rdfs:range ontoksd:KnowledgeType .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#usesProficiencyScheme
ontoksd:usesProficiencyScheme rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentOccurrence ;
                              rdfs:range ontoksd:ProficiencyScheme ;
                              rdfs:comment """Relates an AssessmentOccurrence to a ProficiencyScheme applicable to the interpretation of results from that evaluative event.

In OntoKSD, this association identifies an occurrence-level interpretive framework, including its proficiency categories, descriptors, or numeric classification rules.

Where multiple schemes apply within the same occurrence, the scheme governing each interpretation must remain identifiable through interpretedUsingSchema on the corresponding EvidencedCompetence or EvidencedCompetenceConstituent record. An occurrence-level association does not automatically assign the scheme to every related judgment.

The property has domain AssessmentOccurrence and range ProficiencyScheme. It does not calculate scores, execute classification, assign proficiency levels, or establish judgment validity or competence attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#usesResource
ontoksd:usesResource rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:InstructionalUnit ;
                     rdfs:range ontoksd:EducationalResource ;
                     rdfs:comment """Relates an InstructionalUnit to an EducationalResource included in its pedagogical design.

In OntoKSD, usesResource identifies supporting artefacts such as textbooks, videos, worksheets, rubrics, datasets, simulators, or source code examples. An instructional unit may use multiple resources, and the same resource may support different units.

The association preserves the distinction between planned pedagogical work and the artefacts supporting it. It does not identify the resource as an instructional unit or as a competence constituent.

The intended purpose, applicable version, and any access or usage conditions should be documented where relevant. Mandatory, optional, or conditional use is not determined by this property alone; such requirements must be explicitly described at the appropriate instructional or activation level.

This property has domain InstructionalUnit and range EducationalResource. It records planned use rather than confirming that the resource was accessed, employed in an execution, or effective in supporting learning. It does not automatically classify the resource as collected evidence or establish competence attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#usesScale
ontoksd:usesScale rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                  rdfs:domain ontoksd:ProficiencyScheme ;
                  rdfs:range ontoksd:Scale ;
                  rdfs:comment """Relates a ProficiencyScheme to the Scale providing the numeric range for its score interpretation.

In OntoKSD, usesScale separates the scoring structure from its interpretive meaning. Scale defines the numeric range and any documented increment, while ProficiencyScheme specifies how results are interpreted through intervals and proficiency categories.

A numeric scheme uses one identified scale. Different schemes may share that scale while adopting different interval boundaries, descriptors, or category meanings. Qualitative schemes that do not interpret numeric scores need not use a scale.

Intervals adopted by the scheme must be consistent with the associated scale. This correspondence, valid bounds, and any required score conversion must be explicitly checked rather than assumed from the association.

This property has domain ProficiencyScheme and range Scale. It does not normalize scores, execute classification, establish comparability between schemes, or assign learner proficiency.""" .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme
skos:inScheme rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


