<http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#hasQualityValue> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#evidencedAt
ontoksd:evidencedAt rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  owl:unionOf ( ontoksd:EvidencedCompetence
                                                ontoksd:EvidencedCompetenceConstituent
                                              )
                                ] ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#generatedAt
ontoksd:generatedAt rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:Evidence ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasActivationConstraintDescription
ontoksd:hasActivationConstraintDescription rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:ActivationConstraint ;
                                           rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
                                           rdfs:comment """Records the textual content of a condition, limitation, or requirement represented by an ActivationConstraint.

In OntoKSD, hasActivationConstraintDescription has domain ActivationConstraint and range rdf:langString. Its values are language-tagged descriptions identifying what is required, permitted, limited, or expected within the relevant competence–instructional unit association.

The description should make the condition interpretable by identifying the applicable action, resource, representation, collaboration arrangement, time limitation, or other relevant circumstance. For a conditional constraint, it should also state when the condition applies and what follows when that circumstance holds.

For example, a description may require the use of a designated simulator to construct and test an automaton, or require justification of a modeling choice when multiple representations are permitted.

This property complements hasActivationConstraintType: the description states the condition, while the type classifies its status. Multiple language-tagged descriptions may express the same condition in different languages. Independently applicable conditions should normally be represented by separate ActivationConstraint instances.

The text documents an instructional expectation. It does not itself create a formal logical restriction, execute a compliance check, or establish that a learner has satisfied the condition.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasAlignmentJustification
ontoksd:hasAlignmentJustification rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                  rdfs:domain ontoksd:ExternalCompetenceAlignment ;
                                  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                  rdfs:label "has alignment justification"@en .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasBeginning
ontoksd:hasBeginning rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:RoleDetail ;
                     rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasEnd
ontoksd:hasEnd rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
               rdfs:domain ontoksd:RoleDetail ;
               rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasInstructionalStatement
ontoksd:hasInstructionalStatement rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                  rdfs:domain ontoksd:InstructionalUnit ;
                                  rdfs:range rdf:langString .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasIntegrationDescription
ontoksd:hasIntegrationDescription rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                  rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                                  rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
                                  rdfs:comment """Records a textual explanation of how component competences are intended to contribute to the integrated performance specified by a composite competence.

In OntoKSD, hasIntegrationDescription is used on the composite Competence. Its value should identify the relevant components and explain how their performances are coordinated, combined, sequenced, or mutually constrained to achieve a coherent outcome.

The description should clarify what integration adds beyond the separate performance of the components. For example, when a competence combines problem modeling, implementation, and validation, the description may explain that the implementation must realize the model and that validation must examine the resulting solution against the original problem requirements.

The property complements hasComponentCompetence: component links identify the participating specifications, whereas the description explains their intended integration. The text does not itself create component relationships or formally establish that the described integration is valid.

Values are language-tagged literals, supporting multilingual documentation. Multiple descriptions may be recorded when they address different aspects of the integration.

The property belongs to the specification layer. It describes expected integration rather than collected evidence, an assessment result, or learner attainment. It does not automatically generate assessment criteria, combine constituent assertions, or aggregate judgments concerning component competences.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasOrdinalPosition
ontoksd:hasOrdinalPosition rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain ontoksd:ProficiencyLevel ;
                           rdfs:range xsd:int .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasScore
ontoksd:hasScore rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:AssessmentParticipation ;
                 rdfs:range xsd:double .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasSpecializationDescription
ontoksd:hasSpecializationDescription rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                     rdfs:domain ontoksd:Competence ;
                                     rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
                                     rdfs:comment """Records a textual explanation of how a competence specification refines an explicitly identified base competence specification.

In OntoKSD, hasSpecializationDescription is used on the specialized Competence. Its value should identify the base concerned, describe the retained performance purpose, and explain the narrower scope or delimiting conditions introduced by the specialization.

The description documents the intended meaning of an isSpecializationOf assertion. It does not itself create that relationship or formally establish that the refinement is valid.

Where a competence specializes more than one base, each explanation should unambiguously identify the corresponding base. This property describes specialization at the competence level; it does not provide a separately identifiable record for each specialization relationship.

Values may be language-tagged to support multilingual documentation. The property is descriptive: its content does not automatically generate restrictions, transfer constituent assertions, or establish learner attainment.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasSyllabusText
ontoksd:hasSyllabusText rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                        rdfs:domain ontoksd:Course ;
                        rdfs:range xsd:string .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#hasTaskStatement
ontoksd:hasTaskStatement rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain ontoksd:Task ;
                         rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
                         rdfs:comment """Associates a Task with its textual statement.
    
This property is used to record the linguistic formulation through which the task is expressed in a curricular, instructional, or competency specification context.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#includesLower
ontoksd:includesLower rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                      rdfs:domain ontoksd:ScaleInterval ;
                      rdfs:range xsd:boolean .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#includesUpper
ontoksd:includesUpper rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                      rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topDataProperty ;
                      rdfs:domain ontoksd:ScaleInterval ;
                      rdfs:range xsd:boolean .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#intendedUse
ontoksd:intendedUse rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:EducationalResource ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:string .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isMandatory
ontoksd:isMandatory rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:CourseCompetenceSpecification ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
                    rdfs:comment """isMandatory
Indicates whether the competence associated with a CourseCompetenceSpecification is mandatory within the curricular scope of the Course.

In OntoKSD, isMandatory is used to qualify the curricular status of a competence in relation to a course. When true, it indicates that the competence is considered an essential or required component of the course specification. When false, it indicates that the competence may be associated with the course in a complementary, optional, supportive, or non-central way.

This property does not refer to whether a specific learner must individually demonstrate the competence for approval. Instead, it characterizes the role of the competence within the curricular design of the course itself.

Ontological rationale:
isMandatory is modeled as a qualification of CourseCompetenceSpecification because obligatoriness is not an intrinsic property of either the course or the competence taken separately. Rather, it emerges from the specific curricular relation established between them.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#isTeamBased
ontoksd:isTeamBased rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                    rdfs:domain ontoksd:LearningActivity ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#lowerBound
ontoksd:lowerBound rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                   rdfs:domain ontoksd:ScaleInterval ;
                   rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
                   rdfs:comment """Definition

Specifies the lower numeric bound of a scale interval.

Comment

The property lowerBound identifies the minimum boundary value of a ScaleInterval. Together with upperBound, it defines the numeric range covered by the interval.

For example, in the interval (3.0, 6.0], the lower bound is 3.0.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#maxScore
ontoksd:maxScore rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:Assessment ;
                 rdfs:range xsd:decimal .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#maxValue
ontoksd:maxValue rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:Scale ;
                 rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
                 rdfs:comment """Specifies the maximum numeric value of a scale.

Comment

The property maxValue indicates the upper bound of the numeric range defined by a Scale. It establishes the maximum valid score that may be expressed within that scale.

For example, a scale from 0 to 10 has maximum value 10.0.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#minValue
ontoksd:minValue rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                 rdfs:domain ontoksd:Scale ;
                 rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
                 rdfs:comment """Specifies the minimum numeric value of a scale.

Comment

The property minValue indicates the lower bound of the numeric range defined by a Scale. It establishes the minimum valid score that may be expressed within that scale.

For example, a scale from 0 to 10 has minimum value 0.0""" .


