ontoksd:WrittenExam rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
                    rdfs:label "Written Exam" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#acMandatory
ontoksd:acMandatory rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             ontoksd:ActivationConstraintType ;
                    rdfs:label "mandatory" ;
                    skos:definition "Mandatory denotes an activation constraint in which a specified condition, resource, or requirement must be satisfied for a competence to be considered properly activated, demonstrated, or assessed within a given instructional unit." ;
                    skos:example "The use of a finite automata simulator plays a mandatory constraint when learners are required to construct and validate automata exclusively using a designated simulation tool." .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#acOptional
ontoksd:acOptional rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                            ontoksd:ActivationConstraintType ;
                   rdfs:label "optional" ;
                   skos:definition """optional denotes an activation constraint in which a specified condition or resource may support the performance or assessment of a competence, but is not required for successful task completion or competency demonstration.

Example:

The use of graphical modeling software plays an optional constraint when learners may choose to employ it to visualize automata, while alternative representations are also accepted.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#amAnalytical
ontoksd:amAnalytical rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                              ontoksd:ActivationMode ;
                     rdfs:label "analytical" ;
                     skos:definition """Analytical denotes an activation mode in which a competence is activated through systematic examination, decomposition, or evaluation of structures, behaviors, or properties of a given model, system, or artifact.

Clarification: This mode emphasizes reasoning about existing entities rather than producing new ones.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#amArtifactOriented
ontoksd:amArtifactOriented rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                    ontoksd:ActivationMode ;
                           rdfs:label "artifact-oriented" ;
                           skos:definition """Artifact-oriented denotes an activation mode in which a competence is activated through the production, modification, or use of tangible or digital artifacts that serve as observable evidence of performance.

Clarification: The emphasis lies on the artifact as a product of activity and as a vehicle for evaluation, rather than on the internal cognitive processes that led to its creation.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#amConstructive
ontoksd:amConstructive rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                ontoksd:ActivationMode ;
                       rdfs:label "constructive" ;
                       skos:definition """Constructive denotes an activation mode in which a competence is activated through the cognitive process of creating, assembling, or synthesizing a solution or model. The emphasis lies on the act of construction itself, independent of whether the resulting artifact is preserved or assessed.

Clarification: The focus is on cognitive synthesis and design decisions rather than on the material properties of the produced artifact.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#amIntegrative
ontoksd:amIntegrative rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                               ontoksd:ActivationMode ;
                      rdfs:label "integrative" ;
                      skos:definition "Integrative denotes an activation mode in which a competence is activated through the coordinated articulation of multiple knowledge components, competence constituents, or component competences in order to address a task as a coherent whole. The emphasis lies on semantic synthesis and structured integration rather than on isolated construction, interpretation, or justification alone." .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#amInterpretative
ontoksd:amInterpretative rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                  ontoksd:ActivationMode ;
                         rdfs:label "interpretative" ;
                         skos:definition """Interpretative denotes an activation mode in which a competence is activated through the attribution of meaning to formal representations, models, or artifacts, including explanation, reading, and semantic interpretation.

Clarification: The focus is on understanding and explaining significance rather than evaluating correctness or constructing solutions.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#amJustificatory
ontoksd:amJustificatory rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                 ontoksd:ActivationMode ;
                        rdfs:label "justificatory" ;
                        skos:definition """Justificatory denotes an activation mode in which a competence is atcivated through the articulation and defense of decisions, choices, or solutions using explicit reasoning, criteria, or constraints.

Clarification: This mode emphasizes argumentation and rationale rather than construction or analysis alone.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#applicationDomainKnowledgeType
ontoksd:applicationDomainKnowledgeType rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                ontoksd:KnowledgeType ;
                                       rdfs:label "application domain" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#arCore
ontoksd:arCore rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                        ontoksd:ActivationRole ;
               rdfs:label "core" ;
               skos:definition """core denotes an activation role in which a competence constitutes a central learning objective of an instructional entity and is explicitly targeted by assessment criteria.

Example:

The competence Develop solutions using Turing Machines (C07) plays a core role in an instructional entity whose primary objective is the construction of executable Turing Machine models.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#arExtension
ontoksd:arExtension rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             ontoksd:ActivationRole ;
                    rdfs:label "extension" ;
                    skos:definition """extension denotes an activation role in which a competence is mobilized beyond its foundational scope in order to address extended, integrated, or system-level instructional demands.

Example (usage context)

The competence Develop solutions using Turing Machines (C07) plays an extension role when it is activated in a multi-agent system task that requires coordination of multiple Turing Machines, as formalized through the specialized competence C07.01.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#arSupporting
ontoksd:arSupporting rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                              ontoksd:ActivationRole ;
                     rdfs:label "supporting" ;
                     skos:definition """supporting denotes an activation role in which a competence is mobilized to enable, facilitate, or enhance the activation of another competence that plays a core role, without being the main focus of assessment.

Example:

The competence Test automata using simulators (C03) plays a supporting role when it is used to validate automata developed as part of a task whose core competence is Develop problem solutions using Automata (C01).""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#arTransversal
ontoksd:arTransversal rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                               ontoksd:ActivationRole ;
                      rdfs:label "transversal" ;
                      skos:definition """transversal denotes an activation role in which a competence is mobilized across multiple instructional entities or tasks, often implicitly, without being the primary or explicitly assessed focus in a specific context.

Example:
Basic programming competence plays a transversal role when it is assumed across several computational modeling tasks but is not directly assessed in any single instructional entity.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#attitudeCategory
ontoksd:attitudeCategory rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                  ontoksd:DispositionCategory .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#beliefCategory
ontoksd:beliefCategory rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                ontoksd:DispositionCategory .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#cognitiveSkillDimension
ontoksd:cognitiveSkillDimension rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                         ontoksd:SkillDimension ;
                                rdfs:comment "A SkillDimension emphasizing reasoning, analysis, interpretation, abstraction, evaluation, problem solving, or other cognitive operations. It classifies the nature of the specified capability rather than its taxonomic level or a learner's proficiency. Cognitive involvement may coexist with technical or interpersonal performance." .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#computingSpecificCompetenceScope
ontoksd:computingSpecificCompetenceScope rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                  ontoksd:CompetenceScope ;
                                         rdfs:label "computing specific" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#computingSpecificKnowledgeType
ontoksd:computingSpecificKnowledgeType rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                ontoksd:KnowledgeType ;
                                       rdfs:label "computing specific" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#conditional
ontoksd:conditional rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             ontoksd:ActivationConstraintType ;
                    skos:definition """conditional denotes an activation constraint that applies only under specific conditions or task states, becoming relevant when predefined criteria are met during competence activation.

Example:

The requirement to justify the choice of a Turing Machine variant plays a conditional constraint when multiple variants are available and alternative design decisions are possible.""" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#evFormalArtifact
ontoksd:evFormalArtifact rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                  ontoksd:EvidenceType ;
                         rdfs:comment "FormalArtifact" ;
                         rdfs:label "FormalArtifact" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#evSimulationResult
ontoksd:evSimulationResult rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                    ontoksd:EvidenceType ;
                           rdfs:comment "SimulationResult" ;
                           rdfs:label "SimulationResult" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#evSymbolicAnalysis
ontoksd:evSymbolicAnalysis rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                    ontoksd:EvidenceType ;
                           rdfs:label "SymbolicAnalysis" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#evTechnicalDocumentation
ontoksd:evTechnicalDocumentation rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                          ontoksd:EvidenceType ;
                                 rdfs:label "TechnicalDocumentation" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#evTheoreticalJustification
ontoksd:evTheoreticalJustification rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                            ontoksd:EvidenceType ;
                                   rdfs:label "TheoreticalJustification" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#foundationalCompetenceScope
ontoksd:foundationalCompetenceScope rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                             ontoksd:CompetenceScope ;
                                    rdfs:label "foundational" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#foundationalKnowledgeType
ontoksd:foundationalKnowledgeType rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                           ontoksd:KnowledgeType ;
                                  rdfs:label "foundational" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#interpersonalSkillDimension
ontoksd:interpersonalSkillDimension rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                             ontoksd:SkillDimension ;
                                    rdfs:comment "A SkillDimension emphasizing interaction with other people, including communication, coordination, collaboration, and negotiation. It describes the capability to engage in such interactions rather than the willingness or inclination to do so, which belongs to the dispositional dimension of competence. Interpersonal capabilities may also involve cognitive and technical dimensions." .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#lecture_notes
ontoksd:lecture_notes rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#prerequisiteFunction
ontoksd:prerequisiteFunction rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                      ontoksd:ActivationFunction .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#professionalCompetenceScope
ontoksd:professionalCompetenceScope rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                             ontoksd:CompetenceScope ;
                                    rdfs:label "professional" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#professionalKnowledgeType
ontoksd:professionalKnowledgeType rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                           ontoksd:KnowledgeType ;
                                  rdfs:label "professional" .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#required
ontoksd:required rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#targetFunction
ontoksd:targetFunction rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                ontoksd:ActivationFunction .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#targeted
ontoksd:targeted rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#technicalSkillDimension
ontoksd:technicalSkillDimension rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                         ontoksd:SkillDimension ;
                                rdfs:comment "A SkillDimension emphasizing the practical application of methods, techniques, tools, or procedures. Examples include implementation, construction, configuration, debugging, and deployment. The classification concerns the capability to perform such work, rather than knowledge about a procedure, a particular tool, or evidence of successful execution." .


###  http://purl.org/ontoksd#transversalCompetenceScope
ontoksd:transversalCompetenceScope rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                            ontoksd:CompetenceScope ;
                                   rdfs:label "transversal" .


